.TH POWERGOV 8 "July 2026" "powergov" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
powergov \- systemd service for dynamic CPU governor management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B systemctl
.RB [ COMMAND ]
.B powergov.service
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B powergov.service
is a
.BR systemd (8)
unit that starts
.BR powergov (1)
at boot and keeps it resident across reboots.
The service monitors CPU load every two seconds and adjusts governors on all CPU cores.
.PP
On start, configuration is loaded from
.IR /etc/powergov.conf .
Runtime changes via
.B powergov \-\-battery-safe
are written back to that file.
.SH INSTALLATION
.TP
.B sudo make install-service
Installs the binary, configuration file, systemd unit, bash completion, and man pages.
Enables and starts the service for subsequent boots.
.SH UNIT FILE
The unit is installed as
.IR /etc/systemd/system/powergov.service .
.PP
Key properties:
.TP
.B ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/powergov on
Runs the daemon foreground process managed by systemd.
.TP
.B RuntimeDirectory=powergov
Creates
.I /run/powergov
for the pidfile and control socket.
.TP
.B Restart=on-failure
Restarts the daemon if it exits unexpectedly.
.TP
.B WantedBy=multi-user.target
Enables automatic start on multi-user boot target.
.SH SERVICE MANAGEMENT
.TP
.B systemctl start powergov
Start the service.
.TP
.B systemctl stop powergov
Stop the service gracefully (SIGTERM).
.TP
.B systemctl enable powergov
Enable start at boot (done by
.BR make install-service ).
.TP
.B systemctl disable powergov
Disable start at boot.
.TP
.B systemctl status powergov
Show service state and recent logs.
.TP
.B make service-status
Convenience wrapper for
.BR systemctl status .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/powergov.service
systemd unit file.
.TP
.I /etc/powergov.conf
Service configuration (battery-safe threshold).
.TP
.I /run/powergov/powergov.pid
Daemon pidfile.
.TP
.I /run/powergov/powergov.sock
Control socket for
.BR powergov (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR powergov (1),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd.unit (5)
